From: GT-BE19000AI datapath investigation
Subject: [PATCH] wlshared: globally invalidate DHD D3LUT on bridge station lifecycle

GT-BE19000AI links a model-specific prebuilt DHD object, so editing the
open dhd_pktfwd.c reference source does not reach the shipped DHD module.
The source-built wlshared layer already owns dhd_pktc_del_hook, and the
prebuilt DHD registers that hook to dhd_pktfwd_lut_del().

The DHD delete implementation explicitly treats net_device == NULL as a
global D3LUT-pool lookup. Use that supported path for DHD bridge FDB add
and delete lifecycle events so a stale station MAC is not constrained to
a possibly stale radio/device pool.

This targets the MLO/reassociation stale-state failure where local Wi-Fi
remains healthy while routed Runner/FlowCache forwarding collapses. A
JFFS per-client healer can force a bridge FDB relearn after a positively
identified MLO lifecycle event, causing this hook to run without
deauthenticating the station or globally cycling Runner.

The module load string carries FCD_DHD_D3LUT_REPAIR_V1 so the firmware
build can prove the edited source reached a compiled wlshared binary.
The proprietary DHD prebuilt is intentionally left unmodified.

--- a/release/src-rt-5.04behnd.4916/bcmdrivers/broadcom/net/wl/shared/impl1/wlshared_linux.c
+++ b/release/src-rt-5.04behnd.4916/bcmdrivers/broadcom/net/wl/shared/impl1/wlshared_linux.c
@@ -89,9 +89,28 @@ static int dhd_swdev_event(struct notifier_block *unused, unsigned long event,
 
 	/* function is for dhd device */
 	/* dhd or eth devices */
-	if (dhd_pktc_req_hook && (is_netdev_wlan_dhd(dev) || !is_netdev_wlan(dev)))
+	if (dhd_pktc_req_hook && (is_netdev_wlan_dhd(dev) || !is_netdev_wlan(dev))) {
+		/*
+		 * FCD_DHD_D3LUT_REPAIR_V1
+		 *
+		 * GT-BE19000AI uses a prebuilt DHD object. For DHD FDB add/delete,
+		 * purge by MAC through the exported delete hook with net_device ==
+		 * NULL so PKTFWD searches the global pool instead of trusting a
+		 * possibly stale radio/device mapping.
+		 */
+		if (is_netdev_wlan_dhd(dev) && dhd_pktc_del_hook &&
+		    ((event == SWITCHDEV_FDB_ADD_TO_DEVICE) ||
+		     (event == SWITCHDEV_FDB_DEL_TO_DEVICE))) {
+			dhd_pktc_del_hook((unsigned long)(fdb_info->addr), NULL);
+			return 0;
+		}
+
 		dhd_pktc_req_hook(PKTC_TBL_BRIDGE_EVENT, (unsigned long)(fdb_info->addr),
 			(unsigned long)dev, (unsigned long)event);
+	}
 
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -220,7 +239,7 @@ static int __init wlshared_module_init(void)
 {
-	printk("Loading wlshared Module...\n");
+	printk("Loading wlshared Module (FCD_DHD_D3LUT_REPAIR_V1)...\n");
 
 #if (LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(4, 19, 0))
 	/* register swdev event */
